# =============================================================================
#  ZeroCoin (ZRO) — Anti-Leak Protection Layer
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Goal: no local runtime database, identity store, build output or OS debris
#  can ever be committed or pushed to a remote. Patterns are matched relative
#  to this file (the repository root); the Cargo crate lives in ./zerocoin.
# =============================================================================

# --- 1. Blockchain ledger state & wallet / identity stores -------------------
# Written at runtime by `zerocoind` / `zerocoin-gui` when `--datadir` (or the
# `ZRO_HOME` override) resolves inside the tree:
#   chain.json  -> the full persisted ledger (src/storage.rs::CHAIN_FILE)
#   wallet.json -> the AES-256-GCM sealed keystore, i.e. the private key
chain.json
wallet.json
*.chain.json
*.wallet.json

# Atomic-write siblings (storage.rs / node.rs rename a temp file into place).
wallet.json.tmp
chain.json.tmp

# Throwaway multi-node scratch data used by the devnet guide and demos
# (e.g. `--datadir .\target\zro-a`); a stray in-tree data dir must never ship.
data_node*/
data_node_*/
zro-regtest/
zro-a/
zro-b/

# --- 2. Rust build output & derived artifacts --------------------------------
# The crate is ./zerocoin, so the real artifact dir is ./zerocoin/target — a
# root-anchored `/target` would miss it. `target/` matches at any depth.
target/

# NOTE: Cargo.lock is deliberately NOT ignored. This is a *binary* crate
# (`zerocoind`, `zerocoin-cli`, `zerocoin-gui`), not a library: the lock file
# pins exact dependency versions for reproducible builds and contains no
# secrets. Cargo.toml is likewise tracked.

# --- 3. Editor state, environment files & local scratch ----------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

# --- 4. OS application-directory simulations & platform debris ---------------
# src/datadir.rs resolves state to `%APPDATA%\ZeroCoin` (Windows),
# `~/Library/Application Support/ZeroCoin` (macOS) and
# `$XDG_DATA_HOME/zerocoin` (Linux). Those live OUTSIDE the repository, and the
# sensitive payload they hold (`chain.json` / `wallet.json`) is already blocked
# by section 1, so only fully-qualified in-tree copies need a rule here.
#
# NOTE: a bare `ZeroCoin/` rule is intentionally omitted. `%APPDATA%` is
# meaningless to git, and on case-insensitive filesystems (Windows, macOS) git
# would match a bare `ZeroCoin/` against this project's own crate directory
# `zerocoin/` and ignore the ENTIRE source tree. Only the qualified roaming /
# application-support paths are matched.
**/AppData/Roaming/ZeroCoin/
**/Application Support/ZeroCoin/

# --- 5. General OS / log noise -----------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.log